  title: "Trait laws",
  summary: "Some standard traits carry semantic laws that implementations must preserve even though ordinary type checking cannot prove them.",
  ruleTitle: "A valid signature is necessary but not sufficient",
  ruleBody: "Eq, Ord, Functor, Applicative, Monad, and other documented abstractions define equations or observational properties. Each instance author accepts those contracts in addition to the method types.",
